From a6f0a3370b3f0beef34165bb3c55954e7437eafe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joel Brower <joel.brower@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 00:22:38 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] feat(android): ST Reborn for Android phones and tablets

The desktop app's Go core and frontend, unchanged, in an Android app: speaker
discovery, radio, presets, library, multi-room, Spotify, speaker settings,
network install and speaker updates. The USB-stick route and the desktop
self-updater are hidden, since a phone can do neither.

The page is served from https://wails.localhost, the origin agents already
allow, so no agent change is needed. Android-specific fixes: a net-package
overlay for interface enumeration and DNS on Android 11+, a multicast lock
for discovery, binding to Wi-Fi so a speaker's setup access point is
reachable, and the system pickers for backup and diagnostic files.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016wzfhQtsFu3EKKkUkehQyh
